IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cra-dates`
IMPORT `cra-claims`

-- Compensation to Relatives Act 1897 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in cra-claims.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Dates and amounts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the date`

`married` MEANS `I was legally married to them`
`de facto` MEANS `I was their de facto partner`
`sibling` MEANS `I am their brother or sister`
`half-sibling` MEANS `I am their half-brother or half-sister`
`parent` MEANS `I am their father or mother`
`grandparent` MEANS `I am their grandfather or grandmother`
`in loco parentis parent` MEANS `I stood in loco parentis to them`
`stepparent` MEANS `I am their stepfather or stepmother`
`child` MEANS `I am their son or daughter`
`grandchild` MEANS `I am their grandson or granddaughter`
`stepchild` MEANS `I am their stepson or stepdaughter`
`in loco parentis child` MEANS `they stood in loco parentis to me`
`other` MEANS `none of these`

`not plaintiff` MEANS `I am not the plaintiff on the record, so section 6 puts no duty on me`
`particulars delivered` MEANS `I delivered the particulars together with the statement of claim, as section 6 requires`
`particulars not delivered` MEANS `I have not delivered the particulars section 6 requires together with the statement of claim`

§§ `s 3(1) -- is someone liable`

-- Arguments: wrongful act, neglect or default; could have sued had they lived; serious indictable offence; wrongdoer dead.
#ASSERT `Is someone liable for my relative's death` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "although" a serious indictable offence; "notwithstanding the death of the wrongdoer" (s 6C(1)).
#ASSERT `Is someone liable for my relative's death` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is someone liable for my relative's death` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is someone liable for my relative's death` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Whensoever ... and ..." fails: no.
#ASSERT `Is someone liable for my relative's death` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is someone liable for my relative's death` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is someone liable for my relative's death` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 3, 4, 7, 8 -- can I claim`

-- Arguments: relationship; act before the 1999 amendments; wrongful act; could have sued.
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `married` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `married` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `de facto` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 8: a de facto partner, act before the 1999 amendments took effect.
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `de facto` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `sibling` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `half-sibling` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `parent` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `grandparent` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `stepparent` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `in loco parentis parent` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `child` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `grandchild` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `stepchild` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `in loco parentis child` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Outside the s 4(1) list (fork F1): open.
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `other` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A failed s 3(1) condition beats an open one.
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `other` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `child` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I claim for my relative's death` `married` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 6B(1) -- from what day may I bring it myself`

#ASSERT `From what day may I bring the action myself` (`d` 10 1 2025) EQUALS `d` 11 7 2025
#ASSERT `From what day may I bring the action myself` (`d` 15 9 2025) EQUALS `d` 16 3 2026
-- Year end: 31 December plus six months is 30 June (June has no 31st).
#ASSERT `From what day may I bring the action myself` (`d` 31 12 2024) EQUALS `d` 1 7 2025
-- Fork F5: 31 August plus six months is the last day of February.
#ASSERT `From what day may I bring the action myself` (`d` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `d` 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `From what day may I bring the action myself` (`d` 31 8 2023) EQUALS `d` 1 3 2024

§§ `ss 4(1), 5, 6B -- can I bring the action myself`

-- Arguments: relationship; act before 1999 amendments; executor or administrator; action already brought; day of death;
-- day I plan to bring it.
-- An executor exists and has not sued: the last day of the six months, and the day after.
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action myself` `child` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 10 7 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action myself` `child` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 11 7 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action myself` `child` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action myself` `child` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Across a short February (fork F5).
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action myself` `married` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 31 8 2025) (`d` 28 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action myself` `married` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 31 8 2025) (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No executor or administrator: at once.
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action myself` `parent` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 11 1 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 5: an action already brought.
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action myself` `parent` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 11 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action myself` `child` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 11 7 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a person for whose benefit it is brought.
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action myself` `de facto` TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 1 1998) (`d` 11 1 1998) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action myself` `other` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 11 1 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action myself` `other` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 11 7 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A failed condition beats an open one.
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action myself` `other` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 10 7 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 6 -- particulars`

-- Arguments: plaintiff on the record; day of statement of claim; particulars delivered; day of particulars; every person
-- named; nature of claim stated.
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the section 6 particulars` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not plaintiff`
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the section 6 particulars` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `particulars delivered`
-- The next day is not "together with".
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the section 6 particulars` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 2 3 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `particulars not delivered`
-- Earlier counts as with it (fork F6).
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the section 6 particulars` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 28 2 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `particulars delivered`
-- Not full.
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the section 6 particulars` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `particulars not delivered`
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the section 6 particulars` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `particulars not delivered`
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the section 6 particulars` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 1 3 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `particulars not delivered`

§§ `s 3(2) -- funeral, cremation, headstone`

#ASSERT `Can this funeral or headstone cost be recovered` `the funeral` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this funeral or headstone cost be recovered` `the cremation` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this funeral or headstone cost be recovered` `erecting a headstone or tombstone over the grave` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this funeral or headstone cost be recovered` `the funeral` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can this funeral or headstone cost be recovered` `erecting a headstone or tombstone over the grave` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can this funeral or headstone cost be recovered` `some other cost of the death` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 3(3) -- sums not taken into account`

#ASSERT `Will this money be taken into account` `a sum paid or payable on the death under a contract of insurance` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will this money be taken into account` `a sum paid or payable out of a superannuation, provident or like fund` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will this money be taken into account` `a benefit from a friendly society, benefit society or trade union` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will this money be taken into account` `a pension under one of the listed pension Acts, or an Act amending or replacing one` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Will this money be taken into account` `some other money` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 6A -- payment into court`

-- Arguments: paid in; accepted; issue taken as to sufficiency; jury thinks sufficient.
#ASSERT `Does the defendant win the issue of the payment into court` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the defendant win the issue of the payment into court` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the defendant win the issue of the payment into court` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the defendant win the issue of the payment into court` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the defendant win the issue of the payment into court` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can money paid into court be paid out to me` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can money paid into court be paid out to me` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 4(1) -- dividing the amount recovered`

#ASSERT `How much is left to divide among the relatives` 500000 20000 EQUALS JUST 480000
#ASSERT `How much is left to divide among the relatives` 10000 10000 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much is left to divide among the relatives` 10000 10001 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How much do I receive` 500000 20000 25 EQUALS JUST 120000
#ASSERT `How much do I receive` 500000 20000 33 EQUALS JUST 158400
#ASSERT `How much do I receive` 500000 20000 100 EQUALS JUST 480000
#ASSERT `How much do I receive` 500000 20000 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much do I receive` 500000 20000 101 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How much do I receive` 10000 10001 50 EQUALS NOTHING
